# SPA history fallback (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages).
# Deep links like /hr-policy and /cold-email must serve index.html so the client
# router can resolve the slug — without this, a hard refresh 404s.
# NOTE: API calls go to a separate backend origin (VITE_API_BASE_URL), so there is
# no /api rule here. If you ever serve the API from the SAME origin, add an /api/*
# proxy rule ABOVE this catch-all so it isn't swallowed by the fallback.
/*    /index.html   200
